# --- Agent tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The AI development setup is shared across KaxaNuk repositories and installed by APM, not
# vendored here: the manifest, its lockfile, the modules it downloads and the rules it writes
# into .claude/ all stay out of this repository, which keeps the research tree to research.
.agents/
.claude/
apm_modules/
.mcp.json
apm.lock.yaml
apm.yml

# --- Stage 2: Universe -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable from Investable_Universe.csv (which IS tracked - it is the seed the whole pipeline
# grows from) plus the data provider.
Universe/Security_Master.csv
Universe/Data_Issues.csv
Universe/Provider_Cache/

# --- Stage 3: Data ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing under Data/ is committed except code. Every file here is either downloaded by
# Data/curator.py, derived by Data/refinery.py, or supplied by the user - see README.md.
#
# Today the curator downloads the per-ticker time series and the tradable benchmarks (SPY, QQQ,
# BIL); the KaxaNuk index files and the factor models are dropped in by hand. Once the
# benchmarks-and-factors fabric exists, the curator will fetch those too and this section will
# not need to change.
Data/Curator/Time_Series/*.csv
Data/Curator/Time_Series/*.parquet
Data/Curator/Benchmarks/*.csv
Data/Curator/Benchmarks/*.parquet
Data/Curator/Benchmarks/*.xlsx
Data/Curator/Factors/*.csv
Data/Curator/Factors/*.parquet
Data/Refinery/Time_Series/*.csv
Data/Refinery/Time_Series/*.parquet

# Analyzer output: charts and the signal IC table, both rebuilt by Data/analyzer.ipynb.
Data/Analyzer/Charts/
Data/Analyzer/*.csv

# --- Stages 4-6: Experiments -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Every artefact an experiment produces is rebuilt by its notebook: the weight files, the
# summaries, the engine workbooks (~4.5 MB each) and the charts. None of it is committed. The
# `.gitkeep` negations are what keep the folder skeleton itself in the clone.
Experiments/*/Portfolio/*
Experiments/*/Backtest/*
Experiments/*/Attribution/*
!Experiments/*/Portfolio/.gitkeep
!Experiments/*/Backtest/.gitkeep
!Experiments/*/Attribution/.gitkeep

# --- Nothing binary, anywhere -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Charts, workbooks and papers are all either regenerated by the pipeline or licensed to a person
# rather than to the repository. Keeping them out is what keeps a clone small and its diffs
# readable. Notebook outputs are stripped before committing for the same reason - see README.md.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.parquet
*.zip

# --- IDE --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Credentials and local settings ----------------------------------------------------------
# The templates are tracked; the filled-in files never are.
Config/.env
.devcontainer/.env

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local virtual environment. uv creates it on the first run; nothing in it is source.
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
